    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "7. Like unto the face reflected in a mirror the heart of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "women cannot be caught ( comprehended ); their feeling,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "intricate like the faint mountain-track, cannot be gauged;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "their heart has been described by the wise as fickle like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "water on a lotus-leaf; a woman growing with faults is,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "evidently, like a creeper growing with its poisonous shoots.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "8. Leave aside the question whether a man, wounded",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "while facing the enemy attain victory or heaven; the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "applause of both the armies is, indeed, intensely gratifying",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to the ear.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "9. In sll this collection of exceedingly wonderful things,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "whether of this nature or of such extent, either Varàha or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Ràhu, preeminently stands out as an object of wonder: ( the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "former ) in that he alone bore up the earth when it was sunk",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "in water; the latter, the head-remnant, in that he swallows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "his enemy ( the sun ), and afterwards throws him out.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "10. The earth is bounded by the ocean; that store of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "waters is a hundred yojanas in extent; the sun, ever travel-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ling measures the expanse of the sky;—thus in most cases,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "things are confined within well-defined bounds; but victori-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ous is the intellectual brilliancy of the good ( wise ) that is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "unlimited !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
